 summary:["AKI: prerenal (bland UA, FENa < 1%) / intrinsic (glomerular, tubulointerstitial, vascular) / postrenal","Glomerular: dysmorphic RBC, RBC cast, proteinuria · AIN: sterile pyuria, WBC cast · ATN: muddy brown cast","SLE + AKI + active sediment → lupus nephritis → kidney biopsy (ISN/RPS class)","Nephrotoxin: contrast, aminoglycoside, cisplatin, amphotericin B, tenofovir; endogenous: hemolysis, rhabdomyolysis, myeloma, crystals"],
